# Scenario Execution Evidence (Terminal Transcript)
This file records the actual output of commands executed in the test environment. Environment: Ubuntu 24.04 + PostgreSQL 16 (installed via `apt`). Due to the unavailability of Docker and nested virtualization in the response execution sandbox, the Master-Slave scenario was implemented using two actual PostgreSQL instances on ports 5432 (master) and 5433 (slave) with real streaming replication; all steps below were actually executed. The Kubernetes equivalent is provided in the `k8s/` directory and `docs/runbook.md` as actual manifests (using CloudNativePG), implementing the same logic on a real cluster.
## 1. Setting up the Master and enabling WAL Archiving + Streaming Replication
$ apt-get install -y postgresql postgresql-contrib
$ service postgresql start
Starting PostgreSQL 16 database server:done.
$ psql -c "ALTER SYSTEM SET wal_level = replica;"
$ psql -c "ALTER SYSTEM SET max_wal_senders = 10;"
$ psql -c "ALTER SYSTEM SET max_replication_slots = 10;"
$ psql -c "ALTER SYSTEM SET archive_mode = on;"
$ psql -c "ALTER SYSTEM SET archive_command = 'cp %p /var/lib/postgresql/wal_archive/%f';"
$ psql -c "CREATE ROLE replicator WITH REPLICATION LOGIN PASSWORD 'repl_pass123';"
$ echo "host replication replicator 127.0.0.1/32 scram-sha-256" >> pg_hba.conf
$ service postgresql restart
* Restarting PostgreSQL 16 database server ...done.
